<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Walter von Cronberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1479–<a href="/years/1543">1543</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Walter von Cronberg was German Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> at Mergentheim. After Grand Master Albert secularised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1525, the emperor made him administrator of the grand mastership in 1527, and his successors combined the two offices, ruling the order's remaining lands from Mergentheim in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/walter-von-cronberg.jpg" alt="Walter von Cronberg" width="320" height="487" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WalthervonCronberg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
